    Bug 2016161 - Part 1: Fix browser_ext_windows_create_popup_cookieStoreId.js by using the correct triggeringPrincipal. r=darktrojan,robwu


    As observed in https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D282760#inline-1541035, our behavior
    differs from Firefox when for loading `about:blank`. As pointed out by Rob Wu, we use the wrong
    principal when opening `about` pages or `moz-extension` pages.

    This patch fixes the principal used by the windows API to allow content scripts in
    `about:blank` without using the preference which re-enabled the deprecated behavior.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283245

